protection of the natural environment in the interests of the health or welfare of human beings or animals;

research aimed at preservation of the species;

higher education, or training for the acquisition, maintenance or improvement of vocational skills;

forensic inquiries.

Article 6 U.K. Methods of killing

1. Member States shall ensure that animals are killed with minimum pain, suffering and distress.

2. Member States shall ensure that animals are killed in the establishment of a breeder, supplier or user, by a competent person.

